  "raw_text": "232\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlrw-Matiu19:27\n):\n \nKais, yang nani diara sut lulki swisi man ninam blikri\n \n–\n \nLook, we have left all things behind and\nfollowed you\n \n/ Mira, hemos dejado todo atrás y te hemos seguido)\n\nPri swiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to be free, to release\n \n/ permitir ser libre, liberar\n\nSwi\n \n(v-present participle / participle presente)\n \n–\n \npermitting, allowing, letting, abandoning, quitting, leaving,\nleaving behind, tolerating\n \n/ permitiendo,\n \ndejando, abandonando,\n \ndejando atrás, tolerando\n\nSwih\n \n(v-irregular present participle / participle presente irregular)\n \n–\n \npermitting, allowing, letting, abandoning,\nquitting, leaving, leaving behind, tolerating\n \n/ permitiendo,\n \ndejando, abandonando,\n \ndejando atrás, tolerando\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nSwih\n \nis usually used only in combination with\n \nWaia\n \nor\n \nTikaia\n \n/\n \nSwih\n \ngeneralmente se usa solo en combinación\ncon\n \nWaia\n \no\n \nTikaia\n)\n\nSwih ki\n \n(\nv-irregular present participle / participle presente irregular)\n \n–\n \npermitting, allowing, letting,\nabandoning, quitting, leaving, leaving behind, tolerating\n \n/ permitiendo,\n \ndejando, abandonando,\n \ndejando\natrás, tolerando\n\nSwih tikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive, to pardon, to forget about a matter, to let go and lose\n \n/ perdonar, olvidar un\nasunto, dejar ir y perder\n\nPâtka\n \ns\nwih tikaia sakripaiska l\nâ\nka ba\n \n(\nn/s\n)\n \n–\n \natonement, atonement sacrifice\n \n/\n \nexpiación\n,\n\nsacrificio de\n \nexpiación\n\nSaurka nani Swih\n \nTikaia Yua\n \n(a/t:\n \nP\nâ\ntka Swih Tikaia Yua\n-\nmwb12/20\n)\n \n–\n \nDay of Atonement\n \n/ Día de\n\nla expiación\n\nSwih tikan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPadin lâka\n)\n\nGâd swih tikan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nGod’s forgiveness\n \n/ el perdon de Dios\n\nSaurka nani swih tikan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSaurka swih tikan lâka\n)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness of sins\n \n/ perdon de\npecados\n\nSwih tikanka lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSwih tikanka\n) (n-construct/s-construct)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n\nSwih waia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto abandon and go\n \n/ abandonar e ir\n\nSwin\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasa\ndo\n)\n \n–\n \nquit, left,\n \nabandoned, permitted\n \n/ dejar, izquierda, abandonado, permitido\n\nSwipara\n \n(v-proh)\n \n–\n \ndo not allow\n;\n \ndo not quit\n;\n \ndo not abandon\n;\n \ndo not leave\n;\n \ndo not tolerate\n \n/ no permita; no\nrenuncie; no abandone; no se vaya; no tolere\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/22\n):\n \nBrinka saura nani mita t\nâ\nm bribia swipara\n \n–\n \nDo not allow bad desires to lead you (control you)\n \n/ No\n\npermita que los malos deseos lo guíen (lo controlen)\n)\n\nSwirka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSwika\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething let go, something allowed, something allowed to leave, something\nabandoned\n \n/ algo soltado, algo permitido, algo permitido irse, algo abandonado\n\n(Note/Nota: When this word is combined with a verb, it adds the idea of “to allow, to permit”\n \n/ Cuando esta palabra se\ncombina con un verbo, agrega la idea de \"permitir\")\n\nSwirka daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to do\n \n/ permitir hacer\n\nSwirka munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to do, to allow to do to someone\n \n/ permitir hacer, permitir hacer a alguien\n\nSwirka kunin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to trick, to allow to be fooled\n \n/ permitir engañar, permitir ser\nengañado\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-05/19-stadika21\n):\n \nYawan swika naha tasba sinska lâka mita kunin wan munbiara\n \n–\n \nDo not\nallow the wisdom of the world to fool us\n \n/ No permitas que la sabiduría del mundo nos engañe)\n\nSwirka takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to\n \nhappen\n \n/\n \npermitir que suceda, permitir\n \nque ocurra\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb19\n):\n \nFero ba,\n \nu\npliki nani swika taki waras kabia kaka, ...\n \n–\n \nIf Pharaoh does not allow my people to go, ...\n \n/\n\nSi Faraón no permite que mi gente vaya, ...\n)\n\nSwirka takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to stop\n \n/ permitir parar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg1\n):\n \nSwirka mai takasbiara\n \n–\n \nDon’t allow to stop you\n \n/ No permitas detenerte)\n\nSwirka waia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto let go\n \n/ dejar ir, permitir ir\n\nSwis\n \n(\nv\n-\nimp\n)\n \n–\n \npermit, allow,\n \nlet,\n \nabandon, quit, leave, leave behind\n \n/ permit\ne, permita, permitan,\n \nabandona,\n\nabandone, abandonen,\n \ndeja,\n \ndeje, dejen,\n \ndeja atrás\n, dej\ne\n \natrás\n,\n \ndej\nen\n \natrás\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb88\n):\n \nNaha waitnika nani na swis mahka wabia!\n \n–\n \nLet these men go!\n \n¡Dejen ir a estos hombres!\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf28\n):\n \nP\nȃ\nna pain kum wal aisas bara swis hilp mai munbia\n \n–\n \nTalk to a good friend and let him help you\n \n/\n \nHabla con\n\nun buen amigo y deja que te ayude\n)\n\nTnaya ra swiaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nTnayara swiaia, Nayara swiaia\n,\n \nSnayara swiaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto leave on the side, to leave to the\nside, to allow to go to the side\n \n/ dejar de lado\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nPal dîa luki kan dîa dîa ai tnayara swin ba dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat was Paul thinking about everything that he\nleft to the side (gave up)?\n \n/ ¿Qué pensaba Pablo acerca de todo lo que dejó a un lado (renunció)?)",
